	'preservation_cavity_cards' => "Early | Early cavity — fluoride · sealant | Slight discoloration or enamel damage on the surface. No drilling — <strong>high-concentration fluoride</strong> encourages remineralization. Molars get <strong>sealants</strong> to prevent further decay.\nModerate | Moderate cavity — aesthetic resin filling | Decay has passed the enamel into dentin. <strong>Minimal reduction + tooth-colored resin</strong> restores shape and color. Done in 1–2 visits.\nAdvanced | Advanced cavity — ceramic inlay/onlay | When the cavity is too large for resin alone, a <strong>ceramic inlay/onlay</strong> restores it precisely. Strength, aesthetics and durability. Made in our 13F lab.\n★ Moon Dental specialty | Deep cavity — saving the nerve with pulp capping | When decay is very close to or slightly exposes the nerve, most clinics move straight to root canal or extraction. We first try <strong>pulp capping</strong>: <strong>MTA/Biodentine</strong> forms a dentin bridge so the tooth is <strong>preserved without root canal treatment</strong>. A signature technique of our conservative dentistry team.\nExtensive | Extensive cavity — crown (zirconia · gold) | When the tooth structure is badly damaged, a <strong>crown (zirconia or gold)</strong> after root canal treatment restores strength. Precise fit from our in-house lab.\nPrevention | Preventing recurrence | Check-ups every 6–12 months, scaling, air-flow and fluoride to prevent new decay. Brushing and diet guidance included.",
	'preservation_cavity_callout_title' => '★ What makes us different · Pulp capping',
	'preservation_cavity_callout_body'  => '<p>When decay reaches the nerve, most patients are told to have root canal treatment right away, or in severe cases extraction and an implant. But if the nerve is still alive, it can be given a chance to survive.</p><p>Moon Dental Hospital actively performs <strong>pulp capping</strong>: regenerative materials such as <strong>MTA (Mineral Trioxide Aggregate) and Biodentine</strong> form a dentin bridge over the exposed pulp. When it succeeds, <strong>the natural tooth is preserved without root canal treatment</strong>; if it fails, a root canal can still be done step by step.</p><ul><li><strong>Candidates</strong> — deep decay · micro-exposure of pulp · younger patients · immature permanent teeth</li><li><strong>Materials</strong> — MTA · Biodentine (bio-compatible, regeneration-inducing)</li><li><strong>Team</strong> — performed directly by our conservative dentistry team</li><li><strong>Safety</strong> — can be converted to root canal treatment if it fails</li></ul><p>If you have been advised to extract, or are weighing a root canal for a deep cavity, let us take one more look. <a href="/en/상담예약/">Book a preservation consultation →</a></p>',
	'preservation_pulpcap_eyebrow'  => '⭐ Moon Dental specialty · VITAL PULP THERAPY',
