	'preservation_pulpcap_lead'     => 'When a deep cavity is found, most clinics start root canal treatment immediately. We add one more step. Vital pulp therapy (VPT) treats only the damaged or inflamed part of the pulp and preserves the healthy remainder with MTA or Biodentine, keeping the tooth\'s sensation and lifespan as intact as possible. Indirect and direct pulp capping and partial pulpotomy all belong here.',
	'preservation_pulpcap_when_title' => 'When is vital pulp therapy possible?',
	'preservation_pulpcap_when_list'  => "<strong>Decay removed to just before the nerve is exposed (indirect pulp capping)</strong>\n<strong>Pulp slightly exposed during decay removal (direct pulp capping)</strong> with no infection\n<strong>Small pulp exposure from trauma or fracture</strong> in a young permanent tooth\n<strong>The nerve is still alive (vital pulp)</strong> and there is no spontaneous pain\n<strong>Immature permanent teeth in children and teens</strong> — the nerve must survive for the root to finish growing",
	'preservation_pulpcap_strength_title' => 'Why our vital pulp therapy works',
